    (v_topic_id, '37: Historically, which pathogen was the most common cause of acute epiglottitis before widespread immunization?', '["Haemophilus influenzae type b", "Parainfluenza virus", "Streptococcus pyogenes", "Staphylococcus aureus"]', 0, 'Hib was the classic cause. Today, due to the Hib vaccine, Streptococcus pyogenes and Staphylococcus aureus are increasingly responsible in immunized populations. (Blueprints)'),
    (v_topic_id, '38: What classic radiographic sign is seen on a lateral neck X-ray in a child with epiglottitis?', '["Thumbprint sign", "Deep sulcus sign", "Silhouette sign", "Steeple sign"]', 0, 'The thumbprint sign represents an enlarged, swollen epiglottis protruding into the airway on a lateral neck radiograph. (Case Files Pediatrics)'),
