    (v_topic_id, '161: A 1-year-old female infant presents with a barking cough, hoarseness, and inspiratory stridor. The parents report a low-grade fever and rhinorrhea for the past two days. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Parainfluenza virus", "Haemophilus influenzae type b", "Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV)", "Streptococcus pneumoniae"]', 0, 'Croup is most commonly caused by the Parainfluenza virus. It presents with a seal-like barking cough and inspiratory stridor due to subglottic narrowing. (Nelson Essentials)'),
