    (v_topic_id, '165: Historically, which pathogen was the most common cause of acute epiglottitis before widespread immunization?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes", "Haemophilus influenzae type b", "Staphylococcus aureus", "Parainfluenza virus"]', 1, 'Hib was the classic cause. Today, due to the Hib vaccine, Streptococcus pyogenes and Staphylococcus aureus are increasingly responsible in immunized populations. (Blueprints)'),
    (v_topic_id, '166: What classic radiographic sign is seen on a lateral neck X-ray in a child with epiglottitis?', '["Silhouette sign", "Deep sulcus sign", "Thumbprint sign", "Steeple sign"]', 2, 'The thumbprint sign represents an enlarged, swollen epiglottis protruding into the airway on a lateral neck radiograph. (Case Files Pediatrics)'),
