    (v_topic_id, '348: A 1-month-old snores loudly at night, has witnessed pauses in breathing, and exhibits daytime hyperactivity and poor school performance. Physical exam reveals ''''kissing'''' tonsils. What is the most likely diagnosis?', '["Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) only", "Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA)", "Central Sleep Apnea", "Narcolepsy"]', 1, 'Adenotonsillar hypertrophy is the most common cause of pediatric OSA, which can present atypically with hyperactivity and neurobehavioral issues rather than daytime sleepiness. (Nelson Essentials)'),
    (v_topic_id, '349: Which of the following is the most important modifiable risk factor to prevent Sudden Infant Death Syndrome (SIDS)?', '["Keeping the infant''s room very warm", "Bed-sharing with parents", "Placing the infant supine (on their back) to sleep", "Using a soft mattress with bumper pads"]', 2, 'The ''Back to Sleep'' campaign demonstrated that supine sleep positioning dramatically reduces the incidence of SIDS. Soft bedding, overheating, and bed-sharing are risk factors. (AAP Guidelines)'),
