    (v_topic_id, '358: What classic radiographic sign is seen on a lateral neck X-ray in a child with epiglottitis?', '["Steeple sign", "Deep sulcus sign", "Thumbprint sign", "Silhouette sign"]', 2, 'The thumbprint sign represents an enlarged, swollen epiglottis protruding into the airway on a lateral neck radiograph. (Case Files Pediatrics)'),
