    (v_topic_id, '363: According to asthma guidelines, what is the preferred first-line long-term controller medication for persistent asthma in children?', '["Oral systemic corticosteroids", "Leukotriene receptor antagonists (e.g., Montelukast)", "Inhaled corticosteroids (ICS)", "Long-acting beta-agonists (LABA)"]', 2, 'Inhaled corticosteroids are the most effective long-term controller therapy for all age groups with persistent asthma. (NHLBI/Blueprints)'),
